 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## Agent form tools
+
+The sign-in and sign-up forms expose their existing client-side actions through
+the [WebMCP Declarative API](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/declarative-api).
+In a browser with declarative WebMCP enabled, agents can discover these tools
+while the corresponding page is open:
+
+| Page | Tool | Required parameters |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `/devtools-times/signin` | `sign-in` | `username`, `password` |
+| `/devtools-times/signup` | `sign-up` | `username`, `password` |
+
+The browser derives the input schema from named, labeled, required form controls.
+Both tools wait for the user to submit the populated form. They use the same
+API requests and UI feedback as manual submissions, and return a success or error
+message through `SubmitEvent.respondWith()`. Credentials and API tokens are not
+included in successful tool responses.
+
+Browsers without declarative WebMCP ignore the tool attributes and retain the
+existing form behavior. This experimental API requires browser support; these
+tools are provided by the page, not by an MCP server.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
